{
  "$comment": [
    "PRISM's runtime configuration: read live on every gate run, rendered into",
    "nothing. Changing a value here takes effect on the next invocation, with",
    "no file regenerated. That is what makes it class 1 rather than a template",
    "-- edit it directly; re-rendering only gives back the shipped defaults.",
    "",
    "Rendered from prism.json.in at install by verify/lib/render.py, and read",
    "back by verify/lib/config.sh.",
    "",
    "One key, deliberately. The base branch is the proof knob: the single value",
    "that travels the whole route in this phase -- declared in parameters.json,",
    "rendered here, read by the gates -- so a defect in the mechanism surfaces",
    "with one caller written against it rather than nine (design D6). The other",
    "eight knobs are Phase 2's, and they are absent rather than present-and-",
    "ignored: a key sitting here that nothing reads is a value a consumer can",
    "set and watch do nothing.",
    "",
    "A key a gate needs and does not find here does NOT fall back to a built-in.",
    "The gate denies and names the missing key. See the header of",
    "verify/lib/config.sh for why.",
    "",
    "A SECOND FILE NOW DOES SOFTEN GATES, AND IT IS NOT THIS ONE.",
    ".prism/scope.json says which engines block in which modules, and both the",
    "convention plugins and the push gate read it. R7 was amended for it rather",
    "than evaded -- see 'R7, amended' in docs/prism-verify-requirements.md. The",
    "condition attached is that verify/lib/guard.py compares it, and every other",
    "gate-configuring file, against the base branch and denies a push that",
    "weakened any of them. Nothing about THIS file changed.",
    "",
    "`posture` is the exception to the paragraph above, and the exception is",
    "precise. It is a RECORD of an install-time decision, not a switch: NO GATE",
    "READS IT, and tests/test_base_branch.sh asserts that none does. What it",
    "changes is what prism-doctor compares reality against, and what",
    "`./prism promote --all` flips. A key that softened a gate would be the",
    "runtime escape hatch R7 forbids; a key that records which install was",
    "chosen, so a verifier can report the difference between the record and the",
    "reality, is the opposite of one -- it is how a chosen gap stops being an",
    "invisible gap."
  ],
  "baseBranch": "@BASE_BRANCH@",
  "harness": "@HARNESS@",
  "posture": "@POSTURE@"
}
